Crawd wrote:
>  I came across a new definition in RNG.

RNG stands for Random Number Generator; it is the piece of software,
part of the Nethack source code, that simulates rolling dice whenever a
chance occurrence must be decided within the game.

Since so much of Nethack is randomly decided, people personify the RNG
and call it the Random Number God: an uncaring, all-powerful deity who
sometimes makes good things happen but usually follows it with quick
death.

> Another question I have is about blindfolding, why would you want to
> fight monsters blind?

Some monsters can do nasty things to you if you see them.  To say more
would be a spoiler; but to mention one small thing only, a monster
called a yellow light glows in the dark, and will explode if it gets
near you. The explosion makes you blind for a few dozen turns. But if
you're already blinded or blindfolded when it happens, then no ill
effects occur, and you can see as soon as you remove your blindfold.
There are several other monsters which all have different attacks,
nullifiable by wearing a blindfold.

There is another good reason to wear a blindfold from time to time, but
I cannot figure out how to refer to it without giving it away and
spoiling you.



